<!-- SECTION 2: OVERVIEW / INTRO + TL;DR -->
<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Odoo Accounting in Delhi: l10n_in, GST, and ERP Compliance</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Odoo Accounting Services in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>Odoo accounting = l10n_in config (6 GST slabs, fiscal positions) + NIC e-invoice + e-way bill + GSTR filing from Odoo + TDS/TCS mapping + GSTR-2B matching (Odoo 19). Enterprise Edition required for full GST. 158+ Odoo partners in India but most are IT-only. Patron = CA-led setup + ongoing accounting. From Rs 15,000 setup + Rs 8,000/month. Delhi Rohini office.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Odoo integrates accounting with entire business operations. For a comprehensive overview, see our <a href="/odoo-accounting">Odoo Accounting</a> national guide.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>India Localisation</td><td>l10n_in: 6 GST slabs, fiscal positions, e-invoicing (NIC), e-way bill, GSTR, TDS/TCS</td></tr><tr><td>Enterprise vs Community</td><td>Enterprise required for e-invoicing, GSTR filing, e-way bill, GSTR-2B, TDS alerts</td></tr><tr><td>Setup Timeline</td><td>5-15 business days for full configuration</td></tr><tr><td>Cost From</td><td>Rs 15,000 (GST config) + Rs 8,000/month (ongoing)</td></tr><tr><td>Key Compliance</td><td>GSTR-1 by 11th, GSTR-3B by 20th, e-invoicing >Rs 5Cr, TDS quarterly</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p</p>
                <p>Unlike Tally/Zoho, Odoo is full ERP: accounting is financial outcome of operations. Sales order → delivery → invoice → e-invoice → journal entry in one workflow. 158+ Odoo partners in India but most are IT implementers who leave after config. Patron = CA-led setup AND ongoing compliance. No PT in Delhi. 5 GST zones.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Odoo Accounting?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Definition:</strong> Financial management module within Odoo ERP integrating with Sales, Purchase, Inventory, Manufacturing, HR, CRM on single database. India l10n_in module supports GST, e-invoicing, GSTR reporting.</p><p><strong>Key difference:</strong> Unlike Tally (standalone) or Zoho (cloud accounting), Odoo is full ERP where every operational transaction auto-creates the accounting entry with correct GST. No data re-entry.</p><p><strong>Enterprise required:</strong> Community Edition lacks e-invoicing, GSTR reporting, e-way bill, GSTR-2B matching, TDS alerts. Enterprise mandatory for GST compliance.</p><p>See <a href="/accounting-services">Accounting Services</a> for general accounting.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Odoo Accounting Services in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>l10n_in:</strong> India localisation module. Chart of accounts template, 6 GST slabs, fiscal positions, HSN/SAC, e-invoicing, e-way bill, GSTR, TDS/TCS.</p><p><strong>Fiscal Position:</strong> Auto-switches tax between intrastate (CGST+SGST), interstate (IGST), SEZ, export. Incorrect = every invoice has wrong GST.</p><p><strong>NIC E-Invoice:</strong> API integration via BVM IT Consulting GSP (Odoo 19). IRN generation + QR code on invoices. Mandatory >Rs 5Cr turnover.</p><p><strong>GSTR-2B Matching:</strong> Odoo 19 feature. Fetch supplier GSTR-2B and match against purchase entries for ITC reconciliation.</p><p><strong>Multi-Company:</strong> Separate GSTINs per state. Inter-company transaction rules. Consolidated reporting.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
